-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",100,{
[3169]="7004CF1E\n1\tFind Elves of the Golden Host within Dol Guldur\tElves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.\n2\tTalk to Gladhel within Dol Guldur\tElves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.\n3\tFind Elves of the Golden Host deeper within Dol Guldur\tElves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.\n4\tTalk to Bánoth within Dol Guldur\tElves of the Golden Host can be found within the walls of Dol Guldur.\n5\tExplore the room of shadow at the bottom of the secret stair\tBánoth asked you to investigate the secret stairway his warriors discovered down the slope, behind the door on the left.\n6\tTalk to Sigileth in her hideout\tSigileth is in her hideout deep beneath Dol Guldur.\n",
[3170]="7004CF2F\n1\tDefeat Orcs within Gostador (total: 12)\030Collect hoarded relics within Gostador (total: 8)\030Collect runed tomes within Gostador (total: 4)\tServants of Sauron and evil relics can be found throughout the halls and chambers of Gostador.\n2\tBring the relics and tomes to Sigileth in the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador\tSigileth is in her hideout at the Sorcerer's Stores, in Gostador.\n",
[3171]="700599F1\n1\tLook for Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard\tYou will find Bósi along the southern side of the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.\n2\tTalk to Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard\tYou have found Bósi south of the great pit in Máttugard, studying a troll that has been turned to stone.\n3\tFind the dirty mirror of which Bósi spoke to the south-east\tThe mirror mechanism south of the great pit once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror to the south-east and restore its troll-hindering potential.\n4\tClean the mirror south-east of Bósi's location\tThe mirror mechanism to the south-east once kept the trolls at bay, but now it is filth-covered and non-reflective. Bósi asked you to clean the dirty mirror and restore its troll-hindering potential.\n5\tTalk to Bósi to the north-west in Máttugard\tNow that you cleaned the mirror as he requested, you should return to Bósi in Máttugard, north-west of the cleaned mirror.\n6\tClean the eastern mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur\tBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.\n7\tClean the south-western mirror mechanism at Vâr Nuchur\tBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.\n8\tClean the mirror mechanism north-west of Vâr Nuchur, and down a level\tBósi directed you to the west, where he spoke of more mirrors in need of cleaning.\n9\tTalk to Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur\tSearching for mirrors to clean, you have found Bósi's son Bori north-west of Vâr Nuchur.\n",
[3172]="70066DDA\n1\tComplete 'The Isles: Sirgon the Explorer'\030Complete 'The Isles: The Knight Nauriel'\030Complete 'The Isles: Gimli and Legolas'\030Complete 'The Isles: Keen-eyed Sigileth'\030Complete 'The Isles: The Corsair Daxamat'\tEach member of your crew has gone in search of some way to help, but now many of them are scattered across the various islands that make up the Shield Isles.\n2\tTalk to Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles\tCaebar is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.\n3\tThink it over\tSirgon is interested in your conversation with Caebar.\n4\tTalk to Sirgon by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles\tSirgon has joined you and Caebar by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.\n",
[3173]="70066DE5\n1\tFind the location to the west where Sirgon wants to talk with you\tSirgon has asked to meet you to the west so he can discuss something with you.\n2\tTalk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping\tSirgon is west of Voyage's End, waiting to speak with you.\n3\tWait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts\tSirgon has fallen silent.\n4\tTalk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping\tSirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to continue his tale.\n5\tWait for Sirgon to gather his thoughts once again\tSirgon has fallen silent once again.\n6\tTalk to Sirgon on the rocky outcropping\tSirgon is west of Voyage's End, ready to conclude his tale.\n",
[3174]="7004CF30\n1\tTalk to Galadriel on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin\tGaladriel has cast down the walls of Dol Guldur and laid bare its pits, and now she wishes to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Sigileth on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin\tSigileth is on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.\n3\tTalk to Thranduil on Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin\tThranduil the Elvenking has come to Dol Dhannen, the Hill of Ruin.\n",
[3175]="700599F2\n1\tBori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The first is a short distance to the south of his position.\t\n2\tBori has two locations in mind that might once have served as troll-hoards full of treasure. The second is far to the east, beyond the great pit in the centre of Máttugard.\t\n3\tTalk to Líkmund outside the grodbog-infested troll-hoard, to the north-west\tLíkmund is standing by this one-time troll-hoard, waiting to hear of your discoveries.\n4\tCollect coinpurses from goblins throughout Máttugard (total: 3)\tLíkmund thinks the goblins lurking in the shadowy reaches of Máttugard might have coins they stole during their occupation of Gundabad.\n5\tBring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in Máttugard\tLíkmund asked you to bring the coinpurses to Thettmárr south-west of Maergrind in partial payment of his gambling debt.\n6\tTalk to Bróin at Maergrind, the Noble Gate\tBróin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\n",
[3176]="70066DE6\n1\tTalk to Nauriel at Voyage's End\tNauriel has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles and will surely have a plan.\n2\tNauriel believes you should ask the folk who live in Halrax, on the island of Zamarzîr, what they know about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.\t\n3\tTalk to Daxamat on the eastern side of Halrax, at the bottom of the hill\tDaxamat has come to Halrax in search of more information, and can be found at the bottom of the hill on the eastern side of the city.\n4\tManadhon, the bartender at Halrax, may be willing to tell you about Driftwood, one of the bounty hunters hired by Saklaphêl.\t\n5\tTalk to Nauriel at Voyage's End\tNauriel is back at the Wave-hunter, waiting for information about the bounty hunters recruited by Saklaphêl.\n",
[3177]="700599F3\n1\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind\tDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\n2\tTalk to Durin and ascend to the Steepset with the Gabil'akkâ\tDurin has called for the leaders of the Gabil'akkâ to ascend to the Steepset.\n3\tTalk to Durin at the Steepset\tDurin stands atop the Steepset, considering the progress of his people as they seek to reclaim the halls of Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer at the Steepset\tStáli the Hewer is at the Steepset.\n",
[3178]="70066DEB\n1\tTalk to Caebar at Voyage's End\tCaebar is at the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.\n2\tTravel south-east of the Shield Isles to the Cape of Umbar\tMembers of your crew have gone ahead to the Cape of Umbar, located south-east of the Shield Isles.\n3\tTalk to Gimli on the Cape of Umbar\tGimli is at the Cape of Umbar, waiting for direction.\n4\tTalk to Legolas on the Cape of Umbar\tLegolas is at the Cape of Umbar, waiting for your suggestions about how to proceed with the mission.\n",
[3179]="70047B5D\n1\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to learn what sort of expedition they are setting off on now.\n2\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk with Merry and Pippin now that you have returned to Bâr Thorenion from your meal, and hear their thoughts on the discussion that took place.\n",
[3180]="7005A6A6\n1\tTalk to Víglund\030Talk to Néchek\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should talk to the arguing dwarves in Vérnozal.\n2\tTalk to Igrit\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should talk to Igrit in Vérnozal.\n3\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should search for signs of the goat at the stables in Vérnozal.\t\n4\tSearch for the missing rope\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should search for the missing rope in Vérnozal.\n5\tShow the gift to Néchek\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should show the gift to Néchek in Vérnozal.\n6\tTalk to Víglund\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should talk to Víglund in Vérnozal.\n7\tBring the gift to Igrit\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should bring the gift to Igrit in Vérnozal.\n8\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n9\tComplete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin\tScout-master Ausma and Hórin can both be found at Vérnozal in Máttugard. You should complete a Gundabad Mission with either Scout-master Ausma or Hórin.\n10\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3181]="700472B0\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Hasong in the throne room\tHasong is in King Elessar's throne room.\n3\tThe Haven tavern is on the south-east side of the Third Circle of the city.\t\n4\tExamine Mauthoi's body\tMauthoi's body is on eastern side of the Haven tavern.\n5\tSeveral of the people in the Haven might have seen something when Mauthoi was murdered.\t\n6\tTalk to tavern-worker\tA tavern-worker has begun to clean up some of the blood. Did he see anything?\n7\tLook for bloodstains outside the tavern and follow them\tThe tavern-worker has scrubbed blood-stains near the door, but does the trail continue out of the tavern?\n8\tExamine the discarded knife\030Examine the second victim\tYou found a body and a knife hidden a short distance from the tavern. Is this another victim, or the murderer? Or is he both?\n9\tBring the knife to Dúnor in the Haven tavern\tDúnor is in the Haven tavern.\n10\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n11\tTalk to Duinhir in King Elessar's throne room\tDuinhir is in King Elessar's throne room.\n12\tFind the location where Duinhir believes he last saw his knife\tDuinhir may have last seen his knife at the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle, but he does not really remember.\n13\tTalk to folk near the spot Duinhir described\tA Gondorian man seeks to get your attention on the parapet on the north side of the Fifth Circle.\n14\tConfront Parthadan outside the Dome of the Sun\tParthadan, the Warden of the Green, is outside the Dome of the Sun on the north-east side of the Sixth Circle.\n15\tTalk to Dúnor outside the Dome of the Sun\tDúnor has come with you to apprehend Parthadan.\n16\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3182]="7001466B\n1\tTalk to Brogur and defend the Deep-way\tBrogur is in the Deep-way. The survival of the dwarves in Moria now depends on the ability of you and your allies to defend these locations from attack. You were asked to speak with Brogur first.\n2\tTalk to Stóthkell and defend the Way of Smiths\tStóthkell is in the Way of Smiths. Now that the Deep-way has been secured, you should lend your aid to Stóthkell.\n3\tTalk to Wíli and defend the Twenty-first Hall\tWíli is in the Twenty-first Hall. With both the Deep-way and the Way of Smiths secured, you should head at once to the Twenty-first Hall and aid Wíli in its defence.\n4\tTalk to Bósi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern end of Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have helped to fight off the initial assaults of the Orcs on the barricades of the dwarves, and should report of your success to Bósi.\n",
[3183]="70047293\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Foldgráf in the Hall under the Mountain and go with him to Khazad-dûm\tFoldgráf is assembling a group to come to the aid of the Iron Garrison, in Khazad-dûm.\n3\tTalk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain\tBósi is in the Hall under the Mountain. Khazad-dûm, and much of the Iron Garrison, is lost.\n4\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n",
[3184]="7002161D\n1\tTalk to Radanir at Echad Eregion\tThe next leg of the journey will take the Grey Company to Echad Eregion, and it is there that they will meet up with you again.\n2\tTalk to Fúsi Gem-cutter at Echad Eregion\tFúsi Gem-cutter is at Echad Eregion. Radanir has asked you to speak with Fúsi Gem-cutter about his serious problem, a problem which has brought the Grey Company to a halt.\n3\tFind the site of the attack on Fúsi and Fúni Gem-cutter\tFúsi Gem-cutter's father Fúni was attacked somewhere east of Echad Eregion. Fúsi has asked you to find the site of the attack and determine where his father has been taken by the Ninkoth uruk.\n4\tFind information about the Ninkoth uruks east of the fallen pack\tThe tracks at the fallen pack lead east. It is in that direction that Fúni Gem-cutter must have been taken. You have learned in what direction the Ninkoth uruks have taken Fúni Gem-cutter and should follow the tracks.\n",
[3185]="70013AF7\n1\tBring the rotting pages to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Command, up the eastern stairs within the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Bori has asked you to consult with his uncle Brogur about the Heart of Fire.\n",
[3186]="7000F0F7\n1\tHelp Bori with the task Bósi gave him\030Bring thick branches to Bósi\030Collect thick branches (total: 6)\tThick branches can be found at the base of trees in the area around the Hollin Gate. Bori is likely talking to his friend Bróin at the stairs east of Bósi. Bósi has asked you to collect thick branches with which to make sturdy pick-handles and to help his son Bori with the task of gathering sharpening stones.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is west of the stairs leading up to the foetid lake in front of the Hollin Gate. Bósi is waiting to speak with you now that sufficient materials for new pick-axes have been gathered.\n",
[3187]="70014645\n1\tCollect iron bars (total: 8)\030Collect wooden slats (total: 8)\tIron bars and wooden slats can be found throughout the Flaming Deeps of Moria, where Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai make ready for war. Brogur wants you to collect materials that can be used for making barricades to defend the Twenty-first Hall.\n2\tDefeat Ghâsh-hai Orcs within the Flaming Deeps (total: 20)\tHarass the Orcs of the Ghâsh-hai within the Flaming Deeps, south of Anazârmekhem. Brogur wants you to harrass the Orcs after collecting the materials that can be used for making barricades to defend the Twenty-first Hall.\n3\tBring barricade materials to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have gathered materials for the construction of effective barricades and have also thinned the ranks of the Ghâsh-hai.\n",
[3188]="7000F0F8\n1\tCollect sharp Eregion stones (total: 6)\tStones can be found along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but not every stone is suitably sharp. Bori is waiting for you to bring him enough stones to sharpen the pick-axes needed by the workers unearthing the Hollin Gate.\n2\tBring sharp Eregion stones to Bori\tBori is at the base of the stairs that lead up to the foetid lake in front of the Hollin Gate. Stones can be found along the dry bed of the Sirannon, but not every stone is suitably sharp. Bori is waiting for you to bring him enough stones to sharpen the pick-axes required by the workers unearthing the Hollin Gate.\n",
[3189]="70020999\n1\tTalk to Daervunn at Esteldín\tThe Ranger Daervunn can be found in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger encampment in the North Downs. Halros has told you to next bring your message to Halbarad, but since the Ranger is often away seeing to the elimination of threats, you should speak first to his second-in-command, the Ranger Daervunn.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at Tham Úmdúr\tHalbarad is in Tham Úmdúr, in the shadow of Ost Crithlanc, far to the east of Esteldín, in Nan Amlug East. Daervunn told you that Halbarad has gone to investigate a cave where foes fleeing from Carn Dûm following the defeat of the False King hope to create a new Angmar. If you are to enlist Halbarad's help as part of the Grey Company, you will need to travel to Tham Úmdúr.\n3\tDestroy statue of Amarthiel\030Destroy statue of the Witch-king\030Destroy statue of Mordirith\tThree stone idols of great significance to the Angmarim can be found throughout Tham Úmdúr. Halbarad has already destroyed three of the idols, but three remain, and he wants you to deal with them.\n4\tTalk to Halbarad at Tham Úmdúr\tHalbarad can be found near the entrance to Tham Úmdúr, in the North Downs. You have destroyed three of the idols prized by the Angmarim and should return now to Halbarad, as he asked.\n5\tTalk to Daervunn at Esteldín\tDaervunn is in Esteldín, the hidden Ranger-camp in the North Downs. Halbarad has sent you back to tell Daervunn to gather as many Rangers for the Grey Company as can be spared without jeopardizing the safety of the people of the North Downs.\n",
[3190]="70014754\n1\tCollect Pûlpum Orders from Globsnaga Pûlpum (total: 3)\tPûlpum ensnared by the corruption of the Globsnaga can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone, but especially on and around the underground lake in its depths. Dithaliwenn wants to learn to what purpose Mazog has sent so many of his Orcs to the Foundations of Stone, for it seems to be an uncharacteristic move. She wants you to defeat Globsnaga Pûlpum and wrest away any orders they may still carry.\n2\tBring the Pûlpum orders to Dithaliwenn\tDithaliwenn is in the camp of Gwathrendath, the Shadowed Refuge among the Foundations of Stone. You have collected orders from the corrupted Globsnaga Pûlpum and should bring them to Dithaliwenn in Gwathrendath.\n",
[3191]="70025379\n1\tTalk to Neirin Brehur\030Talk to Penlhun Brehur\030Talk to Siorus Brehur\030Talk to Guladus Brehures\tThe Brehur and Brehures can be found in the Brenin's Hall in Lhanuch. Glynn Brenin has asked you to speak with his advisors about the words of Anirin the messenger and about the events of his rescue.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad in Lhanuch\tHalbarad is among the huts on the western side of Lhanuch. You have spoken with the Brehur and Brehures of Lhanuch and should return to Halbarad with their words as Glynn Brenin wished.\n3\tTalk to Nona in Lhanuch\tNona is in the north-eastern corner of the Dunlending village of Lhanuch. Halbarad has remembered that you did not bring his refusal to Nona and wants you to tell her that he cannot allow her to travel with the Grey Company when they depart.\n",
[3192]="7001AC59\n1\tTalk to Stóthkell in the Heart of Fire\tStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire, off the Way of Smiths, among the Silvertine Lodes. Bósi has asked you to journey to the Heart of Fire to see if the shackles for Mazog have been made.\n2\tBring the mithril shackles to Bróin in the Peaceful Path\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located off Durin's Way. You have collected the shackles to be used to secure Mazog for the journey into Mirkwood and should bring them now to Bróin.\n3\tTalk to Lenglammel in Gwathrendath\tLenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the camp of Elves in the depths of the Foundations of Stone. Bróin has sent you to tell Lenglammel that the dwarves will not bring Mazog through Lothlórien on their way to Mirkwood, skirting the wood instead. He also wants you to express his displeasure with the requirement.\n",
[3193]="70018F0E\n1\tUse Flat Mossy Stone\030Collect Glimmering Beryl\tA stone on which to place Nimpheleg's beryl can be found in the deepest area of Buzun-ghâr. Nimpheleg believes that you can draw out and defeat the source of the rot in Buzun-ghâr by placing a beryl on a stone in the depths of the cave. He warned you to stay near the beryl once you placed it, for only the stone will diminish the ferocity of the master of the rot.\n2\tTalk to Nimpheleg\tNimpheleg is at Lossathrod, the encampment in the upper reaches of Buzun-ghâr. You have drawn forth and defeated the source of the rot within Buzun-ghâr, a diminished spirit: Grawulun the Caerog.\n",
[3194]="70014753\n1\tDefeat Globsnaga Orcs throughout the Foundations of Stone (total: 18)\tOrcs of Mazog's command, corrupted by the sickening evil, can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone. Forglinn has asked you to defeat as many of Mazog's corrupted Orcs, the Globsnaga, as you can. The creatures seem to be mindless, but are still dangerous.\n2\tTalk to Forglinn\tForglinn is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone. You have defeated many of the Globsnaga Orcs, and should return now to Forglinn.\n",
[3195]="7001466C\n1\tComplete Skirmish: Battle of the Deep-way\tBrogur is in the Deep-way. Once you have assembled your allies, you should speak with Brogur. It will not be long before the Orcs arrive.\n2\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Deep-way. You have repulsed the attack on the Deep-way by the Orc hordes, and should speak now to Brogur about the victory.\n",
[3196]="7001466E\n1\tComplete Skirmish: Battle of the Twenty-first Hall\tWíli is in the Twenty-first Hall. The time has come to defend the Twenty-first Hall from attack by the Orc onslaught. Speak with Wíli to arrange the defence.\n2\tTalk to Wíli\tWíli is in the Twenty-first Hall. You have successfully defended the Twenty-first Hall from the Orc attack, and should speak now with Wíli.\n",
[3197]="7001466D\n1\tComplete Skirmish: Battle of the Way of Smiths\tStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire. You should speak to Stóthkell when you have gathered your allies and are ready to man the defences of the Way of Smiths.\n2\tTalk to Stóthkell\tStóthkell is in the Heart of Fire. You have defended the Heart of Fire from attack by the Orc-hordes, and should speak now to Stóthkell.\n",
[3198]="7005AFFA\n1\tTalk to King Thráin at Muru Azog\tKing Thráin can be found at Muru Azog. After the defeat of Azog, King Thráin appears intent on routing the remaining Orcs at Azanulbizar. You should talk to King Thráin.\n2\tInvestigate the gates of Khazad-dûm\030Defeat Ufúrzrak Orcs at Muru Azog (total: 10)\030Defeat Ufúrzrak thrug-hai at Muru Azog (total: 4)\tNud-mekhem, the east-gate, can be found to the west of Muru Azog. Hoping to rout the last of the Orcs at Azanulbizar, King Thráin has asked you to investigate the gates of Khazad-dûm and defeat Orcs of the Ufúrzrak clan.\n3\tTalk to King Thráin and aid in 'A Final Reckoning'\tKing Thráin can be found at Muru Azog. You have driven back the Orcs at Muru Azog and found the remains of Azog being picked by crows. You should talk to King Thráin.\n4\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Amdân\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Amdân. You have witnessed the end of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[3199]="70014752\n1\tHelp Forglinn with his task\030Help Dithaliwenn with her task\tForglinn and Dithaliwenn are in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek. Lenglammel wonders if your fates may be revealed if you help the Elves of her company stand against the darkness.\n2\tTalk to Lenglammel\tLenglammel is in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone beneath Nud-melek. You have aided the Elves of Lenglammel's camp and should speak to her again.\n",
[3200]="70049559\n1\tTalk to Lord Celeborn\tYou should ask Celeborn in the Court of Lothlórien about the ancient text.\n2\tTalk to Glathlírel\tYou should talk to Glathlírel in the Court of Lothlórien.\n3\tGo with Glathlírel to the Rift\tGo with Glathlírel and return to the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu in search of Glorfindel.\n4\tTalk to Lady Galadriel\tYou should talk to Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien, and tell her all that happened in the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.\n",
})
